//// rakun-bpp/node — `Node`, what a template hole and a component's
//// `children` field hold (decisions 191 and 223).
////
//// A closed set: a `string`; a number of any numeric type and a `bool`, each
//// rendered as its `toString()` text, the same on every target; an `Element`
//// (the component of the `ElementBase` context); a list of them. Anything
//// else — a record, an optional (204), a function — is a type mismatch where
//// the value meets a `Node`. `html """…"""` lowers every `{expr}` hole through
//// a `Node` parameter, so the checker refuses what the set does not name.
////
//// `Node` replaces the retired compiler-known `Children` in this track's
//// examples (223); the core's builders take `NodeChildren`, rakun-bpp's list
//// of elements (`element.bp`, decision 804 (4)).

import {element.Element};

pub type Node = string | i32 | i64 | f32 | f64 | bool | Element | Element[];
